WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
In May 2024, fast food and
counter workers in the US

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.860
earned 31,350 dollars a year,

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:13.630
on average. Registered
nurses earned 98,430 dollars.

4
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:18.980
The average across all
occupations was 67,920 dollars.

5
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.590
Both jobs matter.

6
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.340
So why does one pay about three
times as much as the other?

7
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.050
Does pay really track usefulness?

8
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.490
In this mission, you'll see
how a labor market sets a wage,

9
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.840
and how a firm decides
how many workers to hire.

10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.510
Then you'll shift labor
demand in a graph lab,

11
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.210
predict what happens to pay,

12
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.330
and test it.

13
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out what
really decides a paycheck.
